# Typography

Type comes from basecoat's defaults and Tailwind's scale. There is no
custom font loading and no per-component font sizing — hierarchy is
built from a small, consistent set of utilities.

## Type scale

| Role | Utilities | Use |
| ---- | --------- | --- |
| Page title | `text-2xl font-semibold` | One per page |
| Section heading | `text-lg font-semibold` | Card titles, page sections |
| Body | (default) `text-base` | Running text, table cells, form values |
| Supporting | `text-sm text-muted-foreground` | Descriptions, captions, metadata |
| Fine print | `text-xs text-muted-foreground` | Timestamps, counts, badge text |

Component partials already apply the right step — card titles,
stat-card labels, table headers and form labels carry their sizing
internally. Page code mostly needs the page title and body steps.

## Rules

- One `<h1>` per page; headings descend without skipping levels —
  hierarchy comes from the heading element, with the utility classes
  matching it visually.
- De-emphasise with `text-muted-foreground`, not a smaller size, when
  the text is still part of the reading flow.
- Numbers that update or align in columns (tables, stat cards) use
  `tabular-nums`.
- No bold-on-bold: `font-semibold` marks hierarchy, not emphasis
  inside body text. Inline emphasis is rare in clinical UI; prefer
  restructuring the sentence.
- Line length for prose blocks caps around `max-w-prose`; full-width
  text is for tables, not paragraphs.
